      "card_ids": ["C04","C06","C07","C14","C28","C35","C03","C22","C31","C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Additional polar/basic amidine-containing comparators also show poor oral bioavailability: pentamidine poor due to strong basic amidine moieties (C19, C27, C36); emixustat low in humans and low in monkeys/rats (C15, C26, C29).",
      "card_ids": ["C19","C27","C36","C15","C26","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "High-F comparators (arginine/citrulline, atenolol, perindoprilat) and the mouse peramivir record are structurally distinct, species-specific, or mechanistically different and do not override the low-F analog evidence (C02, C05, C08, C10, C11, C16, C18, C24, C30, C32, C34, C37).",
      "card_ids": ["C02","C05","C08","C10","C11","C16","C18","C24","C30","C32","C34","C37"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral AUC/Cmax records for enalaprilat after enalapril prodrug (C38, C41, C42, C47), dabigatran after dabigatran etexilate prodrug (C39, C45, C46, C49), and lacosamide (C40, C43, C44, C48) provide no absolute F or matched oral/IV AUC for the query or a close non-prodrug analog; they are neutral and do not change the prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No fed-state-specific bioavailability data are available for the query or any transferable analog; all relevant records are from no_reported_external_condition.",
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query; the decision relies on structurally similar analogs and physicochemical priors.",
    "L3 records lack IV comparator/absolute F endpoints and mostly concern prodrugs (enalapril, dabigatran etexilate) or structurally unrelated lacosamide.",
    "Transporter-mediated absorption, formulation, and dose effects on the query are unknown.",
    "Species differences, e.g., mouse peramivir oral bioavailability (C34), limit direct human transfer."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: structurally similar amidine/carboxylate zwitterions (DX-9065a F=2–3%, peramivir <3%, C21 not orally viable) plus pentamidine/emixustat polar-basic liabilities and the query's extreme ionization (logD -7.48, TPSA 148.6, neutral fraction 0) affirmatively support F<20%. L3 oral exposure records are neutral/not applicable and do not change the decision; fed-state evidence remains absent, so confidence is moderate."
}

